/-!
# The radial process of a whole-plane GFF and the two-sided Brownian motion of a cone

* `exists_radialProcess`: for a whole-plane GFF `X` (`LQGMetric.IsWholePlaneGFF`), a measurable `C(ℝ, ℝ)`-valued
  version `ρ` of `t ↦ X_{e^{-t}}(0) − X_1(0)`; it is a centred Gaussian process with covariance
  `radCov s t = min(s, t) + (−s)⁺ + (−t)⁺` (a two-sided Brownian motion; Duplantier–Sheffield arXiv:0808.1560 Prop 3.3,
  DMS §4.1).
* `twoSided b b'`: the two-sided path `t ↦ b(t⁺) − b(0) + b'((−t)⁺) − b'(0)`; for independent Brownian motions
  `B, B'` (continuous versions `exists_continuousVersion_brownian`) it is a centred Gaussian process with the same
  covariance (`twoSided_isGaussianProcess`, `twoSided_covariance`).
* `map_eq_of_radCov`: two measurable `C(ℝ, ℝ)`-valued centred Gaussian processes with covariance `radCov` have the
  same law (finite-dimensional Gaussian vectors, QuantumZipper's `WedgeRes.map_eq_of_gaussian_vec`; Kolmogorov
  uniqueness `IsProjectiveLimit.unique`; the Borel σ-algebra of `C(ℝ, ℝ)` is generated by the evaluations, mathlib
  `ContinuousMap.measurableSpace_eq_iSup_comap_eval`).

This is the input of the replacement `X̃ = lateral(X) + W(−log|·|)`; the radial part of `X` and the
two-sided Brownian motion `W` of the cone have the same law.
-/

